{
  "_": [
    "The plan for the Cyrillic font atlases: the retail atlas grows new rows",
    "at the bottom holding one cell per Cyrillic letter, and a glyph table the",
    "port installs at runtime (build_cyrillic_atlas.py writes both; the body",
    "font's sheet was then redrawn at 4x in that layout, cells and baselines",
    "x4, as res/fonts/TempusGothic_texture_0.dds, so its 1x output is the",
    "layout reference and the title font's is what ships). A cell's",
    "shape comes from a box in the Shattered Dimensions PC atlas of the same",
    "typeface (res/fonts/SDPC_*), scaled by its class -- cap: the retail",
    "capital height over the source's, x: the retail x-height over the",
    "source's -- or from a retail glyph (from), flipped or mirrored, with a",
    "crossbar added (bar). desc: rows of the source box below the baseline",
    "(Д, Ц, Щ, ф ...), which become the cell's descent. A letter that looks",
    "like a Latin one is an alias of that glyph's record; a lower-case letter",
    "of the all-capitals title font is an alias of its capital."
  ],
